# TypeScript path aliases (Backend)

**Hard rule:** never use `../` (or deeper) relative imports in `Server/`. Same-folder `./` only. Keep the `.js` extension on local ESM imports.

This applies inside a feature too - e.g. `providers/image/foo.ts` must not `../../prompt.js`; use `server/Modules/.../prompt.js`.

| Alias | Maps to | Use for |
|-------|---------|---------|
| `server/*` | `Server/*` | Any import that would otherwise climb with `../` |
| `^/*` | repo root | Rare paths outside Server |

```ts
// ❌
import { validate } from '../../Helpers/Validation/validate.js';
import { TaxonVisualStatus } from '../../Types/graphql.js';
import { adaptImagePromptForFlux } from '../../prompt.js';
import { ProviderLimitError } from '../providerLimitError.js';

// ✅
import { validate } from 'server/Helpers/Validation/validate.js';
import { TaxonVisualStatus } from 'server/Types/graphql.js';
import { adaptImagePromptForFlux } from 'server/Modules/TaxonVisual/prompt.js';
import { ProviderLimitError } from 'server/Modules/TaxonVisual/providerLimitError.js';
import { TaxonVisualSchema } from './validation.js'; // same folder OK
```

When editing a file, rewrite every reachable `../` import to `server/...` (or `^/...` outside Server) in the same change. Do not leave parent-relative imports “for consistency with neighbors.”

**Exception:** Codegen-emitted files follow `Codegen/codegen.ts` scalar maps - keep those maps on aliases (`^/Codegen/...`, `server/...`) so regenerations stay correct.
